# Report — literalOperand migration (co-locating the LiteralProvenPresent contract)

## Change

`SwiftDecl.hx` hand-built a `SwiftArrayPreparedOperand` for static read-only
array field initializers, asserting `LiteralProvenPresent` inline. That
assertion is sound only while `StaticFieldHelper.validatedInitializer`
(`packages/compiler/StaticFieldHelper.hx:26`) admits literal/construction
forms alone, because `LiteralProvenPresent` bypasses `prepare`'s presence
veto (`SwiftArrayBoundary.hx:222-227`). The contract lived in a different
file from the fact it justified; widening the initializer language would
have silently minted unproven presence facts with no failing test.

Implemented exactly the specified scope:

1. Added `SwiftArrayBoundary.literalOperand(text, sourceType, emptyLiteral,
   nullLiteral)` next to `sourceStorage`. It performs the same three
   derivations the call site did (storage via the shared `sourceStorage`;
   optionality and presenceFact from `nullLiteral`).
2. Documented the contract as a doc comment on that function, immediately
   next to `LiteralProvenPresent`:
   > Contract: this asserts LiteralProvenPresent whenever nullLiteral is
   > false, and that fact bypasses `prepare`'s presence veto below. It is
   > sound only while `StaticFieldHelper.validatedInitializer` keeps the
   > static initializer language literal/construction-only: every admitted
   > form is evaluated eagerly at load, so the storage is provably present
   > without a runtime check. If the initializer language is ever widened
   > (e.g. to admit arbitrary expressions), this constructor must stop
   > minting LiteralProvenPresent for the new forms, or unproven presence
   > facts will be created silently.
3. Rewired `SwiftDecl.hx` to call `SwiftArrayBoundary.literalOperand(rendered,
   init.t, isEmpty, isNull)`, replacing the inline storage/optionality/
   presenceFact derivations (~15 relocated lines).
4. Static fields were NOT routed through `lowerArrayBoundary` (rejected by
   the analysis; needs per-function `SwiftExpr` state and buys nothing for
   literals). No other code touched; no behaviour change intended.

Full diff: `PATCH.diff` (only the two named files; the worktree carries
pre-existing fix-2 changes to other files, which are excluded).

